    "difficulty_level": "H2",
    "difficulty_reason": "After named congruence classification of quadratic/symmetric forms and finite-field character orthogonality, the selected characteristic-two recurrences still require the new rank-constrained block parametrizations, Schur-complement rank descent and trace-sensitive Artin–Schreier evaluation. The second recurrence also requires the full singular leading-block split and two-by-two character cancellation at native483–568, rather than a routine Gauss-sum substitution. Both coupled recurrences form one independent H2 unit, with the original source shorthand disclosed.",
    "source_scope_note": "Only the even-characteristic branch of exact original Lemma 3.4 is selected, with both recurrences counted together as one problem. Full author body is retained as conservative closed context, including form classes, pairing, exact character sums, block representatives and the complete a-nonzero/a-zero split. Other eigenmatrix, code bound, construction and application results remain unselected context. The printed untyped (2s) at native469 is preserved; no type index is supplied by the editor. All-page source/output QA completed; final actual log has zero glyph/reference/citation/stability or box warnings. This is a source-material candidate, not admission or remote-delivery credit.",
    "source_quirks_note": "Native469 and publishedphysical10 print Q^(m-1)_(k-1)(2s), whereas native240/314 index even-rank quadratic-form character sums by the tuple (2s,tau). Required transition to recurrence16 retains that untyped input. No explicit shorthand convention resolving it was found in the authored nearby setup or proof; no editor type-index repair. Complete original human proof is preserved; no mathematical referee conclusion or editorial correction is made.",
